# These files are consumed on Linux (Raspberry Pi). A CRLF checkout on Windows
# breaks them in ways that are annoying to diagnose: bash reports
# "\r: command not found", and systemd silently mis-parses unit directives.
# Pin them to LF regardless of the platform they are checked out on.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.desktop   text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
